OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Driving/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app
targets list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,
misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real,
compiled canonical feature-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**` — where
the sibling P7 pages ship (Admin/Analytics/Automations/Battery/Charging/Dashboard) and
which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups). The
page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Driving/**`, the faithful equivalent
of the prompt's `Features/Driving`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same
reconciliation the sibling AuditLog/DiskForecast/SleepEfficiency logs recorded; it is the
only deviation from the literal prompt path.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is `/drives`. The `AppRoute` enum already carries a `.driving`
case (pathSegment `driving`, Vehicle group, icon `speedometer`). Following the sibling
registration pattern, `AppRouteParser` aliases `/drives` -> `.driving` and
`DrivesListRouteRegistration` hosts `DrivesListPage` on `.driving`, chained into
`\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift (after SleepEfficiency). The page is reachable via the
Vehicle-group sidebar entry and any `/drives` (or `/driving`/`/performance`) deep link.
(Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

