================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DrivesListPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the list state
(loading/empty/error/success) + bulk-delete state over an injectable DrivesDataSource seam whose
value types mirror the web Drive 1:1 (production binds the KMP DrivingStore through the seam). The page
reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle + VehicleSelect/RangePicker/refresh), the sticky summary bar,
search + removable active-filter chips, the six-tile KPI overview (Drives/Distance/Drive-time/Avg-score/
Efficiency/Cost) with current-vs-prior deltas inside a GlassPanel (or its "no drives in range" empty
panel), the metric-switcher trend chart (P3 TSMetricSwitcherChart, never a WKWebView), the collections
pill row (All/Anomalies/Notable/Commutes/Tagged with live counts), the sort controls, the bulk-selection
toolbar with confirm-to-delete, and the date-grouped drive list (per-day header + relative label + summary)
with pagination and the DriveCard rows (selection checkbox, score badge, time/duration/distance-status/
high-speed/low-efficiency badges, start->end route, avg/max-speed/battery-delta/efficiency/cost metrics).
All physical values are SI and convert to the user's unit only at the render boundary via the shared Units
facade + DrivesFormat; the grade ladder, period/prior stats, anomalies/notable/commutes, daily trend, date
grouping and search grammar are pure ports of drivesAggregation.ts/searchQuery.ts, unit-tested + executed
in two harnesses (the full-model one links the real Shared.xcframework). Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency
type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to a pre-existing, out-of-scope
source error in the generated TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift (the single file with any
`error:` across the whole build; ZERO of mine; forbidden to commit-fix).

